    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n15715" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀρτί-φρων</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῐ], <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,</span> gen. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ονος</span>, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄρτιος, φρήν</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>sound of mind, sensible,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὔτε μάλ᾽ ἀ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					24.261
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Med.</u>
				294
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀρτιμελεῖς καὶ ἀρτίφρονας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>R.</u>
					536b
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. . . πλήν</span> . . <i>quite
				in one's senses</i> except . . , <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>IA</u>
				877
			</span></i>: c. gen., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπεὶ δ᾽ ἀ. ἐγένετο . .
				γάμων</span> when he came <i>to full consciousness of</i>
			. . , <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Th.</u>
				778
			</span></i> (lyr.).</div>
